data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"Welcome! A weather app is a great one to build together, and I'm glad you brought it.\n\nHere's how we'll work. First we'll talk through the idea. Then I'll write it up as a short plan for you to approve. After that, a designer will make a look you can click through, and then we'll build it as a web app that works on desktop and phone.\n\nYou can keep this high level and let me make most of the calls, or we can walk through the details. Tell me which you'd like.\n\nTo get started, here are three questions:\n\n1. **Who is it for, and when do they reach for it?** Examples are a quick morning check before leaving the house, planning outdoor activities, or a commuter who needs rain alerts.\n2. **What matters most?** I'd pick one of these:\n   - (a) Simple and glanceable. This is my recommendation.\n   - (b) Detailed forecasts with hourly data, radar and charts.\n   - (c) Something distinctive, such as a playful or beautiful look.\n3. **Do you already picture anything?** This could be saved cities, current location, °C or °F, or a particular style.\n\nAnswer whichever you like. If you'd rather I decide, say \"you decide\" and I'll make sensible choices and list them as assumptions for you to correct."},"finish_reason":null}]}

